ason":2023,"team":"CAR","distance":0.6211,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Frank Reich"},{"season":2022,"team":"IND","distance":0.659,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Frank Reich"},{"season":2023,"team":"NYG","distance":0.6899,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"TB","distance":0.7508,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Dave Canales"}],"defense":[{"season":2024,"team":"DEN","distance":0.3867,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Vance Joseph"},{"season":2022,"team":"ARI","distance":0.3905,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Vance Joseph"},{"season":2023,"team":"DEN","distance":0.4016,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Vance Joseph"},{"season":2025,"team":"ATL","distance":0.4363,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Jeff Ulbrich"},{"season":2024,"team":"NYG","distance":0.4412,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Commanders are 1-4-1 through week 6 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 172 to 132. The offense has been carrying the team, ranking 16th in EPA per play while the defense sits 24th in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the 3rd lowest under center rate and a number of pass rushers that was among the highest in the league.","offense":"The Commanders offense has been about average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Schematically, they stand out for the 3rd lowest under center rate and the 3rd highest shotgun rate in the league. Jayden Daniels has run the passing game, with Stefon Diggs leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Commanders defense has been well below average by EPA allowed per play so far. Its strongest area has been takeaways per game, where it ranks 11th, and its weakest has been success rate allowed, where it ranks 29th. Odafe Oweh has led the way with 3 sacks. Schematically, they have a number of pass rushers that was among the highest in the league.","special":"The Commanders have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 83% of field goals, which is about average. Their salary cap was spread across positions in a fairly typical way. Their secondary was among the oldest in the league.","players":"Jayden Daniels has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 759 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Stefon Diggs and Terry McLaurin leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. The backfield has been a committee led by Jacory Croskey-Merritt and Rachaad White. On defense, Odafe Oweh leads the team with 3 sacks.","coaching":"David Blough is calling the offense and Dan Quinn is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2025 Eagles under Kevin Patullo and the 2023 Panthers under Frank Reich. Their defense looks most like the 2024 Broncos and the 2022 Cardinals, both under Vance Joseph.","trends":"The offense went from 18th in EPA per play in 2025 to 16th so far this season, about where it was. The defense moved from 30th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 24th so far this season, a modest improvement. The biggest change in approach was screen rate, which went from 8% to 5%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}